Package: selectivePredKit
Title: Selective Classification with a Reject Option and Imbalance-Aware
    Evaluation
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Fatih", "Sağlam", , "saglamf89@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Selective classification (classification with a reject option,
    also called abstention) on top of any already-trained probabilistic
    classifier. From class probabilities, or posterior draws of them, the
    package computes uncertainty scores (least confidence, margin, entropy,
    predictive variance, mutual information), learns an acceptance threshold
    from a target score, coverage or performance metric, and applies the
    fitted selector to new data to decide whether to predict or abstain.
    Includes the LABEL set-valued baseline (Sadinle et al., 2019).
    It implements the class-conditional coverage-matching selection and the
    imbalance-aware evaluation measures of Sağlam et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jbi.2026.105084>: class-specific coverage, generalized
    risk, the imbalance accuracy metric, and the areas under the
    risk-coverage curves (AURC, AUGRC, AUAC, AUIC, CA-AURC, CA-AUGRC). The
    package does not train models and does not depend on any modelling
    framework.
